WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
Two streams rise side
by side on Plynlimon,

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.390
in mid-Wales: the Severn and the Wye.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.050
The upper Severn was about
two-thirds conifer forest.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.830
The upper Wye is mostly grassland.

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.270
A dense monitoring
network records the rain,

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.730
and the flow in each stream.

7
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.950
Both get almost the same rain.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.710
Yet the forested hillside
sends less water downstream.

9
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.510
Why?

10
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.310
In this mission, you'll read real
field data from both streams,

11
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.730
and build a water balance.

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.730
Then you'll learn how to measure
a stream's discharge yourself.

13
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:40.020
Your mission: explain why the forested
hillside sends less water downstream.
